  "description": "A new phrase proves itself (13-accounts §6.6, protocol version 10; the money audit of 2026-10-29, M-1). ReplaceRoot (AccountAction tag 7) carries NewRoot {scheme u8, public_key [32], next_digest [32], signature [64]}: the new phrase's first root, whose digest is the phrase's root_digest_0, signs derive(\"Salarium new root v1\", genesis_hash ‖ account ‖ root_digest_0 ‖ next_digest) with Ed25519; the stateless check verifies it for the sender's account and the network; the account moves on to next_digest (root index 1) and the alias goes to derive_id(5, root_digest_0). ReplaceRootV1 (tag 3, the bare digest) is taken by versions 1 to 9 only. From version 10 an address that holds an alias takes itself back by its first transaction: signed by the root its address commits to, with an account action, it pays no fee and clears the alias. A wallet follows an alias at a phrase's own address only to an account whose key event log proves that phrase (proves_phrase).",
